From: Orange Pi 3 PCIe reference build
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: orangepi-3: pin PCIe MAXI rate

The working vendor H6 Linux 3.10 stack programs PCIE_MAXI to 200 MHz.  Pin
only that existing H6 CCU clock on Orange Pi 3, leaving PCIE_AUX inherited.
This isolates the master AXI/data-path clock from the two-clock v11 result.

Do not change the clock parent, PCIe controller driver, reset or power
sequencing, kernel command line, guarded r8169 driver, or any other DT
property.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h6-orangepi-3.dts
@@ -214,6 +214,8 @@
 };
 
 &pcie {
+	assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_PCIE_MAXI>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <200000000>;
 	vcc-supply = <&reg_bldo2>;
 	vdd-supply = <&reg_dcdcd>;
 	slot-supply = <&reg_vcc33_wifi>;
-- 
2.39.5
